    "final_text": "I've fixed the bug: `retry=0` and `include_archived=false` now show up in the URL, and the full suite passes (11 of 11).\n\n**Cause:** in `src/url-builder.js`, the query code skipped any value that looked \"empty\" (`if (!value)`), which also threw away `0`, `false` and `''`. The same check at `src/url-builder.js:137` did this to values inside arrays, so `{ attempt: [0, 1] }` came out as `attempt=1`.\n\n**Fix:** both checks now skip only `undefined` and `null`, the same rule `normalizePath` in that file already uses for path segments. The diff is two lines, and the builder's API is unchanged. Keys are still sorted, and `buildSignedUrl` gets the fix because it calls `buildUrl`.\n\n**Tests:** I added four to `tests/url-builder.test.js`:\n- `buildUrl keeps retry=0 and include_archived=false query values (ISSUE-214)`: the exact case from the issue.\n- `serializeQuery keeps 0, false, and empty string items inside arrays (ISSUE-214)`: covers the array path.\n- `serializeQuery keeps an empty string value as key= (ISSUE-214)`\n- `serializeQuery still omits null and undefined values and array items`: makes sure the fix doesn't start writing `cursor=null`.\n\n**Checks:**\n- **Before the fix:** the three ISSUE-214 tests failed. The first one produced `...?dry_run=true`, which is the bug as reported.\n- **Guard test:** I also removed the new checks entirely, and the `null`/`undefined` test failed as it should. The fix is back in place.\n- **After the fix:** `npm test` passes 11 of 11, run through the dex `run-gate.sh` wrapper since the `dx` command isn't installed here.\n\n**Behavior changes:** an empty string used to be dropped and now comes out as `key=`, and `NaN` now comes out as `key=NaN`. I kept those because they're real values dropped by the same faulty check, but anyone relying on `''` being left out will see a difference. Passing `undefined` or `null` still leaves a key out. Both changes are noted in the `Resolution` section at the end of `ISSUE.md`, along with the fixed code path and the test names.\n\nNothing is committed. The changes are uncommitted on `main`, and the repo has no remote.",
